I can see the issue. Looking at `showNextReveal()`:

```typescript
this.addSkipButton(() => {
  if (proceeded) return;
  proceeded = true;
  this.input.off('pointerdown', proceed);
  if (vid.active) vid.destroy();
  // 10연차: 영상 스킵 시 남은 리빌 전체 건너뛰고 결과 화면으로
  if (this.pullResults.length > 1) {
    this.showSummary();
  } else {
    this.showRevealCard(pulled, def);
  }
});
```

The skip button only appears during character reveal videos and jumps straight to the summary for multi-pulls. When there's no video, the card reveal plays with a 700ms debounce before accepting input, and for 10 pulls it auto-advances after 3.5 seconds instead of waiting for a tap.

The user is reporting that the skip functionality isn't working properly for non-SR characters—they want a skip button available even when there's no video, so they can jump to the summary from the reveal card phase too. I see the issue now—the skip button placement is inconsistent. When characters have videos, the skip button appears during the video playback, but characters without videos skip straight to the reveal card with no way to bypass it. I need to add a skip button directly in `showRevealCard()` for multi-pull scenarios that jumps to the summary screen.

Implementing the skip button in the reveal card phase... I see the issue now—when there's no video reveal, multi-pulls don't have a skip button at all, so I need to add one in `showRevealCard()` that lets players skip the current card and jump straight to the summary screen.

Adding skip button logic... 탭 진행 설정 후, 스킵 버튼을 카드가 표시될 때 바로 보여줘야 하는데, 700ms 디바운스 이후에 정의되는 `advance` 리스너와의 충돌을 피하기 위해 플래그를 사용해서 처리하는 방식으로 정리하고 있다.

Implementing skip button handler... I see the core problem now—when there's no video for a card, the flow skips the video branch entirely and goes straight to showing the card without a skip button, forcing users to tap through each one individually. The fix is to add that skip button to the card reveal function so multi-pulls can be skipped regardless of whether there's video content.

